cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "FPGA AES-GCM / Experimental MACsec Research Prototype"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype of an FPGA AES-128-GCM / experimental MACsec datapath on
  a Corundum-based PCIe NIC, using the AMD/Xilinx Vitis Security Library
  AES-GCM core. Includes a public performance post-mortem (historical ~2.7/2.75
  Gbps baseline, 10G-capable crypto core model, store-and-forward wrapper
  bottleneck) and a security audit showing the revision is not
  production-secure.
authors:
  - family-names: Sun
    given-names: Le
version: "0.2-audited"
date-released: "2026-08-09"
keywords:
  - fpga
  - verilog
  - vitis-hls
  - aes-gcm
  - macsec
  - corundum
  - network-security
